{"accession":"0001193125-26-359442","cik":"0001217286","filer":"JPMorgan Trust I","form":"N-PX","filing_date":"2026-08-21","accepted_at":"2026-08-21T01:35:34.000Z","report_date":"2026-06-30","is_amendment":false,"source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1217286/000119312526359442/0001193125-26-359442-index.htm","first_seen_at":"2026-10-23T21:25:03+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-23T21:25:03+00:00","documents":[{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1217286/000119312526359442/primary_doc.xml","sha256":"0b8d86a610e564d9114575134817f24d536ff7d6ab3228154f21f4989216641b","bytes":28795},{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1217286/000119312526359442/proxyvote.xml","sha256":"2ead305fc32953831faf45609c7f47539483cef4fa0d3a7b9e0aec123acc2527","bytes":59354595}],"cover_fields":{"reportType":"FUND VOTING REPORT","registrantType":"RMIC","periodOfReport":"06/30/2026","amendmentType":"","amendmentNo":"","confidentialTreatment":"N","explanatoryNotes":"A Fund does not have the right to vote proxies for securities on loans over a record date of such proxies. However, if a Funds Adviser has notice of the proxy in advance of the record date, the Funds Adviser may terminate a loan in advance of the record date if the Funds Adviser determines the vote is considered material with respect to an investment, such as when the Funds Adviser believes that its participation in the vote is necessary to preserve the long-term value of the Funds investment or in highly contested issues for which the Funds Adviser believes its vote is important to the Funds strategy. In determining whether a vote is material, the Advisers determination is informed by its responsibility to act in a Funds best interests. In most cases, the Adviser anticipates that the potential long-term value to a Fund of voting shares would not be material and would therefore not justify forgoing the potential revenue the loan may provide the Fund. This may result in proxies being voted by the borrower of the security in a way that would be contrary to how the Funds Adviser would vote if the security had not been lent, including for certain Funds that have strategies to invest in companies that the Funds Adviser believes are sustainable leaders based on the Advisers sustainability criteria or that meet certain other Environmental, Social, or Governance (ESG) criteria. However, in certain instances, the Adviser may determine, in its independent business judgment, that the value of voting outweighs the securities lending revenue loss to a Fund and may therefore recall shares to be voted in those instances."},"parse_status":"parsed","coverage_note":"Structured XML table(s) parsed; confidential/omitted records may exist","vote_chunks":["shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00000.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00001.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00002.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00003.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00004.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00005.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00006.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00007.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00008.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00009.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00010.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00011.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00012.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00013.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00014.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00015.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00016.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00017.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00018.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00019.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00020.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00021.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00022.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00023.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00024.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00025.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00026.json","shards/npx/0001193125-26-359442-00027.jso